post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
==> GulchCE does not include the game data. You need an Xbox disc image
    (.iso or .xiso) of Halo: Combat Evolved, any region.
==> Run "gulchce". At the first start it asks for the disc image and copies
    maps/ from it into ~/.local/share/gulchce (or put a maps/ folder there
    yourself).
==> Everything is in ~/.local/share/gulchce: your settings (config.toml),
    maps/, custom_maps/, mcc_maps/, saves/ (saved games, profiles and the
    map cache), the log (debug.txt) and screenshots.
==> GulchCE cannot play online with OpenCE: they have different network
    versions. Invite links open whichever of the two you started last.
==> Settings and controls: /usr/share/doc/gulchce/LINUX.md
    MCC custom maps: /usr/share/doc/gulchce/MCC.md
MSG
}
